WEBVTT

NOTE Draft cue timing follows measured scene audio and word count. Review spoken word alignment before publication.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Welcome to Resgrid Academy. In this lesson, we will make location information useful

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:09.999
and current. A map can mislead when old positions remain visible or useful

00:00:09.999 --> 00:00:14.999
sites and reference layers are missing. We will explain the features, the setup

00:00:14.999 --> 00:00:18.460
decisions, and a practical way to check the result.

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:24.330
A department adds its stations and hospitals as points of interest and lets

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:29.599
personnel locations expire after 60 minutes so old positions disappear. A current map

00:00:29.599 --> 00:00:34.869
shows where responders and apparatus are and puts important locations in front of

00:00:34.869 --> 00:00:40.139
dispatchers. The examples in this series use a fictional department and are teaching

00:00:40.139 --> 00:00:41.760
scenarios, not default settings.

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:47.690
Mapping. The live map of personnel, units and calls. Set how long locations

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:53.020
stay on the map in the mapping settings. Availability also depends on Mapping.

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:55.480
Check access in the target department.

00:00:56.080 --> 00:01:01.887
Points of Interest. Points of interest such as stations, hospitals and hydrants. Add

00:01:01.887 --> 00:01:07.693
the locations dispatchers need to see. Availability also depends on Mapping. Check access

00:01:07.693 --> 00:01:09.480
in the target department.

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:14.936
Weather zones and alerts. Weather alert zones and alert notifications. Draw the zones

00:01:14.936 --> 00:01:17.550
you cover and choose who is alerted.

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:23.093
Map Layers. Add your own shapes and overlays to the map. Confirm members

00:01:23.093 --> 00:01:28.036
allow location sharing in the Responder app, and decide how long a position

00:01:28.036 --> 00:01:32.979
should stay on the map. Availability also depends on Mapping. Check access in

00:01:32.979 --> 00:01:34.120
the target department.

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:40.080
Live Routing. Directions and routes for responding resources. Confirm members allow location sharing

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:45.440
in the Responder app, and decide how long a position should stay on

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:50.800
the map. Availability also depends on Mapping. Check access in the target department.

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:56.464
Custom map layers. Upload your own map images, such as a campus or

00:01:56.464 --> 00:02:01.529
venue map. Confirm members allow location sharing in the Responder app, and decide

00:02:01.529 --> 00:02:06.593
how long a position should stay on the map. Availability also depends on

00:02:06.593 --> 00:02:09.320
Mapping. Check access in the target department.

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:15.163
Indoor maps. Floor plans and zones for buildings. Confirm members allow location sharing

00:02:15.163 --> 00:02:20.407
in the Responder app, and decide how long a position should stay on

00:02:20.407 --> 00:02:25.650
the map. Availability also depends on Mapping. Check access in the target department.

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:31.456
Routes. Planned routes, such as patrols, and who is assigned to them. Confirm

00:02:31.456 --> 00:02:36.662
members allow location sharing in the Responder app, and decide how long a

00:02:36.662 --> 00:02:41.868
position should stay on the map. Availability also depends on Mapping. Check access

00:02:41.868 --> 00:02:43.470
in the target department.

00:02:44.070 --> 00:02:49.570
For the training scenario, work in this order. Step 1. Review personnel and

00:02:49.570 --> 00:02:55.070
unit location-age settings. Step 2. Add stations and hospitals as points of interest.

00:02:55.070 --> 00:03:00.571
Step 3. Add a relevant map layer, planned route, or weather zone and

00:03:00.571 --> 00:03:01.840
review its audience.

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:08.774
Now verify the result. Check marker age and source, POI placement, reference-layer alignment,

00:03:08.774 --> 00:03:15.107
and the intended weather-alert coverage. A common problem to watch for: Location sharing

00:03:15.107 --> 00:03:21.441
requires client permission. Uploaded floor plans are reference material; verify currency and alignment

00:03:21.441 --> 00:03:23.390
before relying on them.

00:03:23.990 --> 00:03:28.994
Your practice task is simple. Follow a sample unit and compare a recent

00:03:28.994 --> 00:03:33.997
position with a stale position. Record missing POIs and outdated reference layers. Record

00:03:33.997 --> 00:03:39.001
the result, who owns the follow-up, and when it should be reviewed. Use

00:03:39.001 --> 00:03:42.850
the linked feature scripts for the detailed screen recording plan.

